  "visualBrief": "Whole surviving Daulatabad architectural ensemble: all twelve selected native castle/city-defense wall traces and upper-citadel perimeter, their intrinsic bastions/crenellations and mapped gates; complete three-balcony red Chand Minar; summit Baradari white open gallery/dark flanking blocks; Chini Mahal palace-prison gateway; Bharat Mata/Jami Masjid courtyard colonnade and intrinsic Hathi Houz tank; artificial moat retaining/cut-rock edges and its own short crossing. Natural monolith is supplied by an independent frozen terrain field, not a generic cone or invented site slab. Exclude modern town buildings, unrelated temples, standalone cannons/exhibits, vegetation/paths/public landscape, signs/people/vehicles and reconstructed demolished historic wings. Retain full native wall courses/bastion protrusions instead of invented repeating round towers. Real openings at mapped gate points, pointed gate surrounds and dark basalt ramparts. Three balcony minaret with flared supports, serrated parapets and domed crown/finial. Real open pointed arches on projecting white Baradari gallery; ornate Chini gateway with true lower passage and surviving asymmetric crown towers. Open temple courtyard/colonnades and tank/moat voids. Freeze independent whole-site terrain first; natural hill comes from that raw field, never a generic cone. Concealed sections/census/provisional pavilion-palace positions bounded.",
